title: '[pallet-revive] capture long execution traces one window at a time'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The execution tracer collected every step into one buffer, which the allocator rejects past
    `MAX_POSSIBLE_ALLOCATION` (32 MiB), so transactions over roughly 262k steps could not be
    traced at all.

    `ExecutionTracerConfig` gains `step_offset`, which pairs with `limit` to select the window
    `step_offset..step_offset + limit`. Replaying with successive offsets returns a long trace one
    window at a time, and the windows concatenate into the whole: each step keeps the gas, weight,
    storage snapshot and error it would have had in one piece, and every window reports the
    transaction's own totals. A window covers one execution, as `limit` already does, so under
    `trace_block` it applies per transaction.

    At the default `step_offset: 0` the tracer captures what it captured before, with one
    exception: a call whose callee ran past `limit` and then failed is no longer annotated with
    that error, which would otherwise move with the window.

    The window is reached through `ExecutionTracerConfigV2`, selected by a new `TracerTypeV2` and
    carried by new `V3` input payloads of `trace_block`, `trace_tx` and `trace_call`, whose
    `version_declarations` are bumped to `3`. The `V1` and `V2` payloads and the output types are
    unchanged.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `eth-rpc` pages internally. `debug_traceTransaction` and `debug_traceCall` call the runtime
    with an increasing `step_offset` until a window comes back short, so transactions past the
    former step ceiling can now be traced; each window replays the block up to the transaction
    again. Windows are sized from what the previous one measured, and one the node refuses as too
    large is halved and asked again, up to eight attempts.

    A trace is still bounded by what one response can carry. Where the steps do not fit within
    `--rpc-max-response-size` the request fails rather than return a prefix indistinguishable
    from a whole trace, and the error names the largest `limit` that would succeed; a `limit` the
    response can hold is returned as asked for.
    `debug_traceBlockByNumber` is unchanged.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-types
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: major
